"text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)-452du":{"title":"accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/accessibilityrotor(_:textranges:)-452du","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)-452du","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityRotor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Text","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4TextV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"textRanges","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Range","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sn","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS5IndexV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">]) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}]}}}